cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived panel, please cite both the software and the accompanying article."
title: "peatfire-eval: panel construction and evaluation-protocol experiments for district-month fire severity forecasting in Indonesia"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data for a study of how evaluation-protocol choices affect model
  rankings in fire hotspot prediction. Builds a district-month panel of VIIRS S-NPP
  active fire detections for the 14 districts of West Kalimantan and the 55 districts of
  Indonesian Kalimantan, evaluates seven forecasting models under a 2x2 design crossing
  the test distribution with the discrimination metric, and tests whether models and
  their rankings transfer between provinces under two severity targets.
type: software
license: MIT
